SUMMARY:Wildflower seed collecting with the TRCA
DESCRIPTION:Join Toronto Master Gardeners in partnership with the Toronto Regional Conservation Authority and learn how to identify\, sustainably collect and save native wildflower seeds . \nThe morning begins with a short walk into the Meadoway from the Jonesville Allotment gardens to sustainably collect native wildflower species. Then you will learn how to dry\, sort and save the seeds from the flower heads you have collected. Participants can keep a limited amount of the seeds they collect for use in their own garden. \nFree tickets available through Eventbrite – https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/wildflower-seed-collection-in-the-meadoway-with-toronto-master-gardeners-tickets-1996668121099?aff=ebdssbcategorybrowse \n 
URL:https://www.torontomastergardeners.ca/event/wildflower-seed-collecting-with-the-trca/
LOCATION:Jonesville Allotment Gardens
END:VEVENT
